  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JERUSALEM: FROM CRISIS MANAGEMENT TO CONFLICT RESOLUTION</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Jerusalem: From Crisis Management to Conflict Resolution aims to 1) Systematically gather data and analyse developments on the ground in East Jerusalem, and to report on these to key decision-makers; 2) Engage key decisionmakers with concrete achievable policy proposals geared to restore Jerusalem as a credible permanent status issue to be resolved through negotiations; 3)  Transform the regional normalization process into a platform to enhance the engagement of the Arab world in support of preserving the feasibility of the two state solution in Jerusalem; 4) Engage prominent religious leaders in Israel, Palestine and beyond, on the faith dimension of the conflict (most importantly status quo and custodianship issues on Haram al Sharif/Temple Mt).</narrative>
  </description>
